        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> June 24, 2026</p>

        <p>Paybots, Inc. ("Paybots," "we," "us") builds agentic payment infrastructure. This policy describes what we do with information when you visit <a href="https://paybots.io">paybots.io</a>, use our demo and verification tools, or use Paybots products and services (together, the "Services").</p>

        <h2>Marketing site (paybots.io)</h2>

        <h3>No third-party tracking</h3>
        <p>The marketing site is designed to make <strong>no third-party network requests</strong> during normal browsing. Fonts are self-hosted. We do not use analytics pixels, advertising tags, or social widgets. A Content-Security-Policy header restricts scripts, styles, fonts, images, and connections to paybots.io (with one exception below).</p>

        <h3>What we do not use on the marketing site</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>First-party or third-party analytics or advertising cookies</li>
            <li>Session replay or heatmap tools</li>
            <li>Third-party form relays or lead-capture services</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Demo video</h3>
        <p>The product demo is embedded from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code> only after you click to play. Until then, no YouTube resource is loaded. YouTube may set cookies or collect data according to its own policies once the embed loads. Your browser may store a local preference that you have unlocked the demo so you are not prompted again on the same device; that value stays in your browser and is not sent to us.</p>

        <h3>Seal verification tool</h3>
        <p>The <a href="/verify/">Verify</a> page parses and cryptographically checks underwriting seals entirely in your browser. Purchase data you paste is not uploaded to our servers.</p>

        <h3>Hosting logs</h3>
        <p>Our static site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub and any CDN in front of the site may log standard request metadata (IP address, user agent, requested URL, referrer, timestamps) as part of operating the infrastructure. We do not receive those logs directly and do not use them for marketing or profiling.</p>

        <h3>Email</h3>
        <p>If you email us (for example via <a href="mailto:hello@paybots.io">hello@paybots.io</a>), we receive whatever you choose to send: your address, message contents, and any attachments.</p>

        <h2>Paybots products and services</h2>
        <p>When a merchant, partner, or end user interacts with Paybots beyond the public marketing site — for example through an integrated checkout agent, underwriting workflow, or merchant dashboard — we process additional information needed to operate the service.</p>

        <h3>Information we process</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account and contact data</strong> — names, email addresses, company details, and credentials for authorized users.</li>
            <li><strong>Agent conversations</strong> — messages and context from AI agents interacting with Paybots on behalf of users or merchants, including purchase intent, mandate checks, and underwriting decisions.</li>
            <li><strong>Transaction and purchase data</strong> — cart contents, amounts, currency, fulfillment details, and related metadata needed to validate and guarantee payments.</li>
            <li><strong>Underwriting seals</strong> — cryptographic attestations we issue about approved purchase terms, including hashes and signatures described in our public rulesets.</li>
            <li><strong>Support and operational records</strong> — correspondence, audit logs, and diagnostic data we generate to secure and improve the Services.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>How we use it</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Provide, secure, and improve agentic payment and underwriting features</li>
            <li>Validate purchases against user mandates and merchant rules</li>
            <li>Issue and verify underwriting seals</li>
            <li>Respond to support requests and legal obligations</li>
            <li>Detect abuse, fraud, and security incidents</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>AI processing</h3>
        <p>Paybots uses large language models — including Anthropic Claude models accessed through <strong>Amazon Bedrock</strong> — to interpret agent conversations and support underwriting decisions. Conversation content submitted for processing is transmitted to our cloud infrastructure and to Bedrock under our agreements with those providers. We configure these services for our operational use; they are not used to train public models on your data through our Bedrock configuration.</p>

        <h3>Staff access</h3>
        <p>Authorized Paybots employees and contractors may access conversation logs, transaction records, and related data when reasonably necessary for support, debugging, security review, compliance, or product development. Access is limited by role and subject to internal policies.</p>

        <h3>Service providers</h3>
        <p>We use infrastructure and subprocessors to run the Services — including cloud hosting, payment processors, identity providers, and the AI providers described above. They process data on our instructions and under contractual confidentiality and security obligations. We do not sell personal information.</p>

        <h3>Retention</h3>
        <p>We retain information for as long as needed to provide the Services, meet legal requirements, resolve disputes, and enforce agreements. Retention periods vary by data type and customer configuration.</p>

        <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict certain processing of your personal information, or to object to processing and receive a portable copy. To exercise these rights, contact <a href="mailto:hello@paybots.io">hello@paybots.io</a>. We may need to verify your identity before responding.</p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>We use administrative, technical, and organizational measures appropriate to the nature of the data we process. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure.</p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>The Services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.</p>

        <h2>International transfers</h2>
        <p>We operate in the United States and may process information there and in other countries where we or our providers operate.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top will change when we do. Material changes to how we treat marketing-site visitors will be reflected here.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:hello@paybots.io">hello@paybots.io</a>.</p>

